    "summary": "High‑energy 1982 Kiel show with scorching CC Rider, solid Terrapin jam & rare Stagger Lee",
    "review": "The August 4, 1982 gig at St. Louis’ Kiel Auditorium is a quintessential early‑‘80s Dead night – high voltage blues, a handful of deep cuts and a second‑set that still manages to surprise. The first set fires on a blistering “C.C. Rider” and a tight “Brown Eyed Women”, with Jerry’s vintage lead work and Brent’s bright piano/organ driving the band forward. “Row Jimmy” and “Never Trust A Woman” keep the momentum rolling, even as Bob’s vocals wobble on a few numbers later in the set. The second half delivers a memorable “Terrapin Station > Jam > Drums” sequence that showcases the rhythm section’s swing, followed by a classic “U.S. Blues” encore. Highlights also include a rare, well‑played “Stagger Lee” and an unexpectedly strong rendition of “Looks Like Rain”. While some mixes bury Phil’s bass and a few vocal spots miss the mark, the overall performance is solid, energetic, and worth digging into.",
