    "band_performance": {
      "Jerry": "Vintage blues leads on “C.C. Rider”, “Brown Eyed Women” and “Row Jimmy”; solid throughout, acting as a perfect foil to Brent’s piano during the jam sections.",
      "Phil": "Bass underpins every groove but is often buried in the mix; still provides the essential low‑end drive for the set.",
      "Bob": "Early vocal ferocity gives way to occasional off‑notes on “Looks Like Rain” and other tracks, yet his improvisational spirit adds character.",
      "Keys": "Brent Mydland shines with a pop‑piercing intro on “Brown Eyed Women”, expressive Yamaha electric grand on the Terrapin jam, and generally strong piano/organ textures all night.",
      "Drums": "Bill Kreutzmann and Mickey Hart lock in a steady, swinging foundation; especially effective during the “Terrapin Station > Drums” segment."
